[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Stable independent junction charge and domain admission

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-JUNCTION-SMALL-CHARGE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve small finite depletion and transport charge
STATEMENT: >>>
Independent accepted-step audits shall preserve finite junction charge near zero
voltage rather than lose it through subtraction from one. For grading zero and
zero transit time, reconstructed displacement shall agree with C*(Vnew-Vold)/h.
Transport charge shall form the physical current before multiplying by transit
time, avoiding an overflowing TT*IS intermediate when TT*I is finite.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/audit_charge_boundaries.rs small_linear_junction_charge_is_not_lost_by_subtraction_from_one
and zero_transport_charge_does_not_overflow_a_discarded_parameter_product.
The expected results are the closed-form constant-capacitance and zero-current
laws. Extreme finite-parameter tests qualify arithmetic, not a physical device.
Implementation: src/audit.rs independent_junction_charge and independent_element_charge.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-JUNCTION-CONTROL-DOMAIN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reject unrepresentable or unsupported Early charge domains
STATEMENT: >>>
An available fixed-step junction audit shall reject nonfinite differential BC control,
nonfinite Early modulation and nonpositive forward Early charge-domain factors,
including at zero or reverse BE bias. Unrepresentable reconstructed charge
shall return a typed error. Fixed-step backward Euler and nonlinear trapezoidal
adapters shall propagate these errors without publishing a passing report.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: early_control_domain_is_validated_even_at_zero_or_reverse_be_bias,
including finite node voltages whose difference overflows. Stable domain
admission is independent of whether the forward-diffusion branch is active.
Implementation: src/audit.rs and src/audit_configured.rs. This does not qualify
nonlinear stored energy, which remains explicitly unavailable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-JUNCTION-TRANSITION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Use the declared forward continuation at the junction transition
STATEMENT: >>>
At the represented transition FC*VJ, independent junction audits shall use the
forward continuation's constant defined by FC, rather than recompute FC as
(FC*VJ)/VJ. Rounding that quotient near the depletion singularity shall not
silently change the selected piecewise law or its boundary charge.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: depletion_transition_uses_declared_fc_not_a_rounded_reconstructed_ratio.
Grading 3/4 permits an independent nested-square-root integral. The retained
seed2026111906 first sample exercises a one-ulp quotient change with a material
charge difference. Default audit tolerances are retained.
<<<
